Stop the busy walk after 64 providers

The panel shows one thread locking the same service again and again inside
_adjustBusy and that service never returning to zero, so the provider chain
almost certainly loops.  Cap the walk before taking the lock, so nothing is held
when it stops.
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
index 6d7dd7e..5043bdc 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
@@ -5327,11 +5327,15 @@ IOService::_adjustBusy( SInt32 delta )
 	UInt32      result;
 	bool        wasQuiet, nowQuiet, needWake;
 
+	int nio_hops = 0;
 	next = this;
 	result = __state[1] & kIOServiceBusyStateMask;
 
 	if (delta) {
 		do {
+			if (++nio_hops > 64) {
+				break;
+			}
 			if (next != this) {
 				next->lockForArbitration();
 			}
